;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; Four independent authorities are cited, not one: GLEIF (the global LEI
;; system), Belgium's Kruispuntbank van Ondernemingen / Banque-Carrefour des
;; Entreprises (KBO/BCE, the national commercial register the Federal Public
;; Service Economy administers), the United Kingdom's Companies House, and
;; Australia's Business Register. The last three are not picked because they
;; happened to agree -- they are the registration authorities GLEIF itself
;; names, on this entity and on its children, reached by following GLEIF's own
;; RA pointers.
;;
;; THE SUBJECT'S OWN REGISTER ANSWERS HERE. GLEIF records this LEI as
;; registered at RA000025 as 0417.497.106. RA000025 resolves, at GLEIF, to the
;; Crossroad Bank of Enterprises. Asked for that enterprise number, KBO Public
;; Search returns ANHEUSER-BUSCH INBEV -- so unlike a catalog that can only cite
;; the LEI system's copy of a national identifier, the identifier here is read
;; back from the national register that issued it.
;;
;; Three joins are load-bearing and are checkable only against those
;; authorities' own bodies:
;;
;;   * Enterprise number 0417.497.106. KBO returns the name, the registered
;;     seat, the legal form, and a start date of 2 August 1977. GLEIF publishes
;;     creationDate 1977-08-02 for the same LEI. The two systems agree on a date
;;     neither of them is the source of.
;;
;;   * Company number 11642142. GLEIF lists AB INBEV INVESTMENTS HOLDINGS
;;     COMPANY 2 LIMITED among this LEI's direct children and records it as
;;     validated at RA000585, which GLEIF resolves to Companies House. Asked for
;;     11642142, Companies House returns that company, incorporated 25 October
;;     2018, SIC 64209 (activities of other holding companies). Companies House
;;     has no LEI field and no view of GLEIF.
;;
;;   * ACN 071 508 702. GLEIF lists FBG FINANCE PTY LTD (AU) as a direct child,
;;     validated at RA000014, which GLEIF resolves to ASIC. Asked for that
;;     number, the Australian Business Register returns FBG FINANCE PTY LTD,
;;     ABN 32 071 508 702, an Australian Private Company active since 1 November
;;     1999. Note the register cited is the ABR (Australian Taxation Office),
;;     NOT ASIC itself: the ABR republishes the ASIC company number alongside
;;     the ABN, and it is the ABR that answers an unauthenticated GET. This
;;     corroborates the number at a second Commonwealth register, and it is not
;;     a claim to have re-read ASIC's own file.
;;
;; WHY STATUS ALONE CANNOT CARRY THESE ROWS. Measured 2026-08-20, each authority
;; answers 2xx for a WRONG identifier:
;;   * KBO with nummer=0417497107 -> HTTP 200, a 9,154-byte error page
;;   * KBO with nummer=0400378485 -> HTTP 200, a different real company
;;     (COLRUYT GROUP)
;;   * Companies House with company/11642143 -> HTTP 200, a different real
;;     company (HARROP LEGAL LTD)
;;   * ABR with id=071508703 -> HTTP 200, a page reading "Invalid"
;;   * GLEIF filtered by registeredAs=0417.497.107 -> HTTP 200, "total":0
;; So for every one of these rows it is the substring, not the HTTP status,
;; that is doing the work. That is the property the gate exists to hold.
;;
;; IDENTITY ROWS vs ATTRIBUTE ROWS. Not every row discriminates on its own, and
;; pretending otherwise would be the same dishonesty as trusting the status
;; code. This was measured by mutation on 2026-08-20, by repointing each block
;; at a REAL peer -- not at a nonexistent identifier, which is the easy case --
;; and counting what stayed green:
;;
;;   * GLEIF, all 40 subject-structure URLs repointed at SOLVAY
;;     (549300MMVL80RTBP3O28), chosen because it is the most adversarial peer
;;     available: Belgian, RA000025, ACTIVE, ISSUED, R85P, FULLY_CORROBORATED,
;;     region BE-BRU -- every attribute this catalog records. 29 rows DRIFTED,
;;     11 stood: conformityFlag, corroborationLevel, entity status ACTIVE,
;;     registration status ISSUED, jurisdiction BE, region BE-BRU, legalForm
;;     R85P, registeredAt RA000025, the relationship type
;;     IS_DIRECTLY_CONSOLIDATED_BY, and the two parent-exception categories.
;;     All eleven are true of SOLVAY as well.
;;   * KBO, repointed at COLRUYT GROUP (0400378485). 15 of 18 rows DRIFTED;
;;     3 stood -- the Dutch and English legal-form rows and NACE-BEL 70.100,
;;     because Colruyt is also a naamloze vennootschap with head-office
;;     activity.
;;   * Companies House, repointed at 11642143. 4 of 5 rows DRIFTED; the
;;     incorporation date stood, because 11642143 is HARROP LEGAL LTD, a
;;     company incorporated the SAME DAY -- adjacent company numbers are issued
;;     together, which makes an incorporation date the weakest discriminator
;;     this register offers. That row is kept and labelled, not deleted, and
;;     two reverse-lookup rows were added beside it so the block no longer
;;     leans on it.
;;   * ABR, checked against MONAKA PTY LTD (ACN 000 000 019). Only the entity
;;     type stood; the name, the ACN, the ABN and the 1999 activation date all
;;     failed.
;;
;; So 16 of the rows below are ATTRIBUTE rows: they say what is true of
;; whatever entity the URL names, and they mean something only because the
;; IDENTITY rows in the same block pin which entity that is. Each one says so
;; in its own :cite/claim. The gate still fails as a whole in every case above,
;; which is the property that matters; this note exists so no reader mistakes
;; an attribute row for an identification.
;;
;; ENCODING. Substrings are chosen from the RAW response body, and the hosts do
;; not agree on how to encode anything. api.gleif.org escapes every solidus as
;; \/ and all non-ASCII as \uXXXX, so no GLEIF row here matches a URL or an
;; accented local name -- the RA row matches the pure-ASCII
;; "Kruispuntbank van Ondernemingen" rather than "Banque-Carrefour des
;; Entreprises", whose French text GLEIF delivers unescaped but whose sibling
;; fields do not. kbopub and abr.business.gov.au emit &nbsp; INSIDE the values,
;; so the seat is "Grote Markt&nbsp;1" and the ABN date is
;; "01&nbsp;Nov&nbsp;1999"; matching "Grote Markt 1" with a plain space finds
;; nothing. No substring in this file contains a backslash. A normalised form
;; would hide which body was read.
;;
;; TWO LANGUAGES OF ONE REGISTER. KBO Public Search is cited twice, in Dutch and
;; in English, because the two renderings disagree in a way that matters. The
;; Dutch page gives the seat as "Grote Markt 1, 1000 Brussel"; the English page
;; gives the same seat as "Grand-Place 1, 1000 Bruxelles". GLEIF publishes
;; "Grand-Place 1" / "Bruxelles" -- the French form -- for a record whose
;; legalName language it declares as "nl". The English rows are therefore not a
;; duplicate of the Dutch rows: they are the ones that establish that GLEIF's
;; address string is a rendering KBO itself serves, and not a translation
;; introduced somewhere between the two.
;;
;; A NOTE ON THE 2016 RESTRUCTURING. KBO reports that this enterprise number
;; replaces 0649.641.563, closed since 10/10/2016, and that the entity was
;; absorbed by 0649.641.563 (Newbelco SA/NV) on 10 October 2016 -- the vehicle
;; through which the SABMiller combination was carried out. Both statements are
;; on the register page and both are cited below. They are recorded because a
;; reader checking 0417.497.106 against older sources will meet the other
;; number, not because this catalog is asserting a reading of the transaction.
;;
;; Deliberately NOT cited, and why (all measured 2026-08-20):
;;
;;   * VIES, the European Commission's VAT information exchange system, which
;;     confirms BE 0417497106 as "NV Anheuser-Busch InBev" at Brouwerijplein 1,
;;     3000 Leuven -- a genuinely independent EU-level authority, and an
;;     interesting one because that address is the operational seat, not the
;;     registered seat KBO and GLEIF publish. It is not cited because it is not
;;     deterministic. Over 30 consecutive GETs it returned the entity name 20
;;     times; the other 10 answered HTTP 200 with "isValid" : false,
;;     "userError" : "MS_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQ" and "name" : "---". A citation to
;;     it would DRIFT about a third of the time for a reason that has nothing
;;     to do with this entity. Worse, VIES echoes the submitted number back in
;;     every response, including the failures: a row asserting
;;     "vatNumber" : "0417497106" would have passed on all 30 attempts, ten of
;;     them while VIES was reporting that it had answered nothing at all. That
;;     is the exact shape of a check that cannot tell "measured and fine" from
;;     "could not measure", so no VIES row appears here in any form.
;;   * The National Bank of Belgium's Balance Sheet Central, which holds this
;;     entity's filed annual accounts. ws.cbso.nbb.be answers HTTP 401
;;     ("missing subscription key") and the consult.cbso.nbb.be page for
;;     0417497106 answers 200 with a 5,344-byte JavaScript shell containing
;;     neither the enterprise number nor the name.
;;   * The Belgian Official Gazette (Moniteur belge / Belgisch Staatsblad).
;;     www.ejustice.just.fgov.be answered HTTP 500 to the enterprise-number
;;     query form and HTTP 404 to the result path; the one variant that
;;     returned 200 delivered a search page carrying neither the number nor
;;     the name.
;;   * Luxembourg Business Registers (www.lbr.lu), the RA000432 that GLEIF
;;     names for three of this LEI's direct children. It answered HTTP 429 to a
;;     single unauthenticated request, so the Luxembourg children are cited
;;     from GLEIF only.
;;   * Chile's Servicio de Impuestos Internos, the RA000787 GLEIF names for
;;     CERVECERIA CHILE S A. zeus.sii.cl resolves and answers 200, but the
;;     contribuyente endpoint returned a 92-byte body carrying neither the RUT
;;     nor the name; www.cmfchile.cl does not resolve from the environment this
;;     gate runs in. That is a reachability fact about the gate, not a
;;     judgement about the registers.
;;   * The directors. The KBO page lists fifteen named natural persons holding
;;     legal functions, with the dates of their appointments. No claim in this
;;     catalog needs them, so none is cited and none is reproduced here. The
;;     same rule applied to the Belgian entity applies to the foreign children.
;;   * www.ab-inbev.com is the company's own site, not a register, and is not
;;     cited for any claim here. It is the source of the privacy policy this
;;     repository archives; that archive is checked separately, and the two
;;     must not be confused. Measured 2026-08-20, that archive is sound: the
;;     recorded sha256 reproduces from the recorded text, the text carries no
;;     404 marker, and the source URL still answers HTTP 200 with a privacy
;;     policy.
;;
;; Independent third-party archive. Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
;; sponsored by ANHEUSER-BUSCH INBEV.

